        "effect": "none",
        "speaker": "narrator",
        "actor": "lin_yue",
        "text": "The driver beside Yue had a wife working in the dye yards west of Bitter Wells. He sent money home every second crossing and complained that his son could now beat him at counting stones. Another worker said he was saving for a roof, then admitted that he had been saving for the same roof for five years. Their stories crossed without asking Yue for her own. At last she offered a small memory of the west kiln, where damp firewood made everyone accuse the sky. The driver asked whether the sky had ever paid compensation.",
